    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="0229" n="1279" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/7–1152: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Embassy in India</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d728-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-07-11T18:28:00-04:00">July 11, 1952—6:28
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. While Dept realizes Nehru’s remarks (urtel 155)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d728-f2"/> probably constitute
                    rejection Pak proposals, it is not clear whether
                        Nehru gave you a specific answer to
                    transmit Karachi. If Nehru authd you
                    transmit substance of his remarks to Karachi Dept assumes your approach is terminated and Warren may now convey msg to PM. On other hand if
                        Nehru did not specifically indicate
                    reply to be transmitted Dept suggests in your
                    discretion you see Nehru again and ask him
                    what he wld like you to report back to Karachi. While this may not affect his
                    apparent position it will serve purpose impressing further upon him seriousness
                    his failure respond to a generous offer. Likewise in view great importance these
                    talks it is essential record be clear. As you aware Graham not expected proceed with his negots until such time as
                    your approach completed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d728-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d728-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated for information to Karachi (priority), London, and New
                    York.</p>
            </note>
